<div class="content-page">
  <div class="content-page__inner">
    <h1 class="content-page__title">Changelog</h1>
    <p class="content-page__intro">A record of major updates, new features, and fixes.</p>

    <div class="changelog">

      <div class="changelog__entry">
        <div class="changelog__header">
          <h2 class="changelog__version">v2.2.1</h2>
          <time class="changelog__date">October 2026</time>
        </div>
        <span class="changelog__tag changelog__tag--fix">Fixes</span>
        <ul class="changelog__list">
          <li>No text in the lessons or on the site is cut short with "…"</li>
          <li>Before Error is pressed, the correction is shown in full whenever it fits; on a small screen, when it does not, the panel says "Press Error to see the correction" instead</li>
          <li>The exercise details under the title wrap onto a second line rather than being cut off</li>
          <li>Search results show each page's full description</li>
          <li>Pre-K shape drills no longer show an oval, which looked too much like a circle; the shapes offered are circles, squares, triangles, and rectangles</li>
          <li>On phones, a double tap no longer zooms the page, and taps on the child's screen register at once; pinching to zoom still works</li>
          <li>On an iPhone, tapping the child picker or a text box no longer zooms the page in</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="changelog__entry">
        <div class="changelog__header">
          <h2 class="changelog__version">v2.2.0</h2>
          <time class="changelog__date">October 2026</time>
        </div>
        <span class="changelog__tag changelog__tag--minor">Clearer scripts</span>
        <ul class="changelog__list">
          <li>Every line the parent reads in Pre-K, Kindergarten, First Grade, and the Bridge has been reread and rewritten where it was stiff, unclear, or ungrammatical</li>
          <li>Corrections now give the reason for the answer, such as the rule for a shape, the count that gives a total, or the working of a two-digit problem, and end with the same question the child was asked</li>
          <li>Confirmations no longer repeat a whole count or a long answer back to the child</li>
          <li>Story problems use "he" or "she" after the first mention instead of repeating the name, and ask a full question</li>
          <li>Number agreement is fixed throughout ("one dot", "one ten", "a one", "an eight")</li>
          <li>Button names in the instructions match the buttons on screen</li>
          <li>Length questions now ask about shorter as well as longer, and digital clocks are explained by their numbers rather than by clock hands</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="changelog__entry">
        <div class="changelog__header">
          <h2 class="changelog__version">v2.1.0</h2>
          <time class="changelog__date">October 2026</time>
        </div>
        <span class="changelog__tag changelog__tag--minor">One screen</span>
        <ul class="changelog__list">
          <li>Lessons, tests, practice, and the placement test fit on one screen without scrolling, on phones, tablets, and computers</li>
          <li>The teacher's panel puts the exercise title and step on one line, keeps the buttons on one row, and makes the type a little smaller when a step has a lot of text</li>
          <li>The level and lesson, and each exercise title, are shown in full rather than cut off</li>
          <li>The correction shows as a short reminder until Error is pressed, then in full</li>
          <li>Long counting answers are shown to the teacher as numerals so that skipped numbers are easy to spot</li>
          <li>Finish, results, and start screens fit on one screen, and test results are listed by part with the lessons to reteach</li>
          <li>Rows of pictures, place-value blocks, and digital clocks now fit on narrow phone screens</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="changelog__entry">
        <div class="changelog__header">
          <h2 class="changelog__version">v2.0.0</h2>
          <time class="changelog__date">October 2026</time>
        </div>
        <span class="changelog__tag changelog__tag--major">Rebuilt program</span>
        <ul class="changelog__list">
          <li>The 150-lesson, seven-phase program is replaced by three levels: Pre-K (100 lessons), Kindergarten (140), and First Grade (150), plus an optional 20-lesson Bridge to Second Grade</li>
          <li>Lessons are built from skill tracks that run side by side, with new teaching, two lessons of firming, and spaced review</li>
          <li>Every new step is taught with a model, a lead, and a test; every correction states the answer and the rule</li>
          <li>New content: shapes and solids, position words, measurement, sorting, patterns, numeral writing, teen numbers, number families, the equal sign, every kind of story problem, time, graphs, halves and fourths, and optional coins</li>
          <li>Firm and Error marking, starting an exercise over, and a delayed retest of missed items at the end of each lesson</li>
          <li>A mastery test after every tenth lesson, with reteaching links for any part not passed; a placement test</li>
          <li>Printable worksheets for every lesson, and printable cards and mats</li>
          <li>Practice for every skill track, drawn from what the child has been taught; a fact review that tracks each fact</li>
          <li>A new teacher dashboard with test results, error patterns, a fact chart, and notes</li>
          <li>Removed streaks, scores, grade words, and effusive praise</li>
          <li>A build-time check that stops any lesson that shows a number before it is taught, lacks a model, lead, and test, or leaves a skill unreviewed too long</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="changelog__entry">
        <div class="changelog__header">
          <h2 class="changelog__version">v1.0.0</h2>
          <time class="changelog__date">April 2026</time>
        </div>
        <span class="changelog__tag changelog__tag--major">Initial Release</span>
        <ul class="changelog__list">
          <li>150 fully scripted lessons across 7 phases with ~2,400 teaching steps</li>
          <li>Direct Instruction methodology: ~10% new material, ~90% review per lesson</li>
          <li>Natural, varied teacher scripts with multiple phrasing options per step</li>
          <li>68 math concepts from counting to two-digit arithmetic</li>
          <li>25 interactive practice sets covering all 7 phases (341 problems)</li>
          <li>Flashcard system with customizable filters by phase, type, and difficulty</li>
          <li>Interactive visual aids: dot patterns, number lines, tally marks, place value charts</li>
          <li>Teacher/child split-screen lesson view</li>
          <li>Client-side search (Ctrl+K) across all lessons and pages</li>
          <li>Dark mode with toggle in header and lessons</li>
          <li>LocalStorage progress tracking with export/import</li>
          <li>Multiple learner profile support</li>
          <li>Keyboard shortcuts for lesson navigation</li>
          <li>Offline support via service worker with three-tier caching</li>
          <li>PWA install prompt for app-like experience</li>
          <li>Responsive design for mobile, tablet, and desktop</li>
          <li>Landscape mode with side-by-side layout</li>
          <li>RSS feed, XML sitemap, PWA manifest, SEO meta tags</li>
          <li>Open source under MIT license</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="guide-section" style="margin-top:var(--space-2xl)">
